1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,375
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:04,470
(GROANS)

3
00:00:04,538 --> 00:00:07,133
SOFIA: We could've had
a good thing, you and I.

4
00:00:07,774 --> 00:00:08,774
(GUNSHOT)

5
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:11,440
- You!
- Yeah.

6
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:13,513
Me.

7
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,180
When I get out of
here, I'm gonna confess.

8
00:00:16,483 --> 00:00:18,850
My connection
with Sofia. All of it.

9
00:00:18,919 --> 00:00:22,412
No, you wanna pay
your debt, you live with it.

10
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:24,089
It's what the city needs.

11
00:00:24,391 --> 00:00:25,911
RA'S: <i>When I brought
you back to life,</i>

12
00:00:25,993 --> 00:00:28,326
<i>I asked you to be my
eyes and ears in Gotham.</i>

13
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:30,796
<i>You became so much more.</i>

14
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:33,163
- Let her go, now.
- No!

15
00:00:33,734 --> 00:00:35,362
- I'll never go with you.
- No!

16
00:00:35,469 --> 00:00:36,630
(SCREAMS)

17
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:38,831
<i>You killed her!</i>

18
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:41,484
BRUCE: So, now,
you're gonna return it?

19
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:44,967
What am I supposed to say?
"I stole your jewelry. Sorry."

20
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:46,206
Sometimes, that's enough.

21
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,280
Can you do it?

22
00:00:48,282 --> 00:00:49,282
TABITHA: <i>Migraine still?</i>

23
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,664
BARBARA: <i>It's like I've been
hit in the head with a brick.</i>

24
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,017
(BARBARA BREATHES HEAVILY)

25
00:00:57,591 --> 00:00:58,868
PENGUIN: You
could escape anytime.

26
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:00,121
You're planning something.

27
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:03,095
Something spectacular.

28
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:04,697
But, when we're done,

29
00:01:04,765 --> 00:01:09,100
the world out there,
that'll be the asylum.

30
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:20,238
(CHUCKLES)

31
00:01:30,624 --> 00:01:32,286
(BUZZING)

32
00:01:44,137 --> 00:01:45,901
("FOOL FOR YOU"
PLAYING ON WALKMAN)

33
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:20,137
Get back in your bunk, Tetch.

34
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:23,310
(INAUDIBLE)

35
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:27,670
Don't even try hypnotizing me. I
can't hear a word you're saying.

36
00:02:33,787 --> 00:02:36,086
I'm not talking to you!

37
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:41,021
- I'm talking to her.
- (GASPS)

38
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:45,698
Jeez. Tortuga. You almost
gave me a heart attack.

39
00:02:47,034 --> 00:02:49,469
Wait. Where the hell
are your headphones?

40
00:02:52,239 --> 00:02:53,239
(CHOKES)

41
00:02:57,577 --> 00:02:58,577
Did I do it right?

42
00:02:58,679 --> 00:03:00,875
Right as rain, in
the plain in Spain.

43
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:17,791
Knock, knock, called the cock.
Time to rise and wield your scythe.

44
00:03:22,669 --> 00:03:27,266
CRANE: I fear I will require
a moment more, Mr. Tetch.

45
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:29,366
Our moment is fleeting,
my dear Mr. Crane.

46
00:03:29,576 --> 00:03:31,670
Its wings desperately beating.

47
00:03:34,247 --> 00:03:35,545
(SIZZLING)

48
00:03:45,092 --> 00:03:49,359
There, now, scarcely
a drop spilled.

49
00:03:49,863 --> 00:03:52,423
Shall we, Mr. Tetch?

50
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:54,897
Let us be at pains, Mr. Crane.

51
00:03:58,472 --> 00:04:00,031
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

52
00:04:07,214 --> 00:04:09,410
(ALARM BLARING)

53
00:04:14,888 --> 00:04:18,256
When I say "three hairs
past a freckle," gentlemen,

54
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:21,294
I do not mean five hairs past.

55
00:04:21,795 --> 00:04:23,787
Let's do better next time, hmm?

56
00:04:23,897 --> 00:04:26,332
Mind both P's and Q's, Valeska.

57
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:29,460
We are not your militia
to be becked and called.

58
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:33,938
I dread to think where
you'd be without us.

59
00:04:34,007 --> 00:04:38,809
Boys, boys, let's not squabble
too early in our partnership.

60
00:04:39,246 --> 00:04:42,216
There'll be plenty of time to
stab each other in the backs later.

61
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:47,585
But for now, stick to Jerome's plan,
and everyone will get what they want.

62
00:04:47,788 --> 00:04:51,452
An earthly kingdom of terror.

63
00:04:51,558 --> 00:04:54,687
A piece of Gotham
pie both sky and high.

64
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:58,755
That's the spirit, boys.
Think big. And kinky.

65
00:04:58,999 --> 00:05:00,365
(ALARM CONTINUES BLARING)

66
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:04,429
And lose the weirdo. She's
giving me the heebie-jeebies.

67
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:08,969
Your work is done, my
dear. Your race all run.

68
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:10,971
Glad to be of help.

69
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,446
(CHOKES)

70
00:05:19,519 --> 00:05:21,147
Much better. Now,

71
00:05:21,621 --> 00:05:25,080
to free the rest of our cronies,
and blow this pop stand.

72
00:05:30,797 --> 00:05:32,663
(ALL SHOUTING)

73
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:42,106
(WHOOPING)

74
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:58,750
(ALL CHEERING)

75
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,819
Onward, march!

76
00:06:13,907 --> 00:06:15,637
(POLICE SIREN BLARING)

77
00:06:22,816 --> 00:06:24,717
Sure you're up for
this, Captain Gordon?

78
00:06:24,851 --> 00:06:25,875
I'll manage.

79
00:06:25,986 --> 00:06:27,978
Picked a hell of a night
to come back on the job.

80
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,784
- How many got out?
- Eighty-seven.

81
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,688
The entire violent ward.

82
00:06:31,758 --> 00:06:33,638
Yeah, we rounded up
most of the serious nutjobs,

83
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:35,787
the guys that think they're
walruses and whatnot.

84
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:39,765
Ephram Snow, child murderer,
Daedalus Boch, mutilator,

85
00:06:39,866 --> 00:06:42,893
Erasmus Rayne,
cult killer... All at large.

86
00:06:42,969 --> 00:06:45,489
The surviving guards think your
old buddy, Tetch, was behind it.

87
00:06:45,538 --> 00:06:49,031
No. This big, this insane,

88
00:06:49,109 --> 00:06:51,738
Jerome Valeska put this together,
and there'll be more to come.

89
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:55,439
Got a lot of nervous
cops out here tonight

90
00:06:55,548 --> 00:06:57,244
who are thinking
along the same lines.

91
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,118
And I know what you're thinking.

92
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:02,886
Why not tell them the truth?

93
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:07,451
About Sofia, and the Pyg,
get it all out in the open.

94
00:07:07,794 --> 00:07:09,405
I've kept my mouth
shut like you told me to.

95
00:07:09,429 --> 00:07:12,058
Good, and I'm telling
you again. Don't slip.

96
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:16,127
Go over there and be
big Jim Gordon, hero cop.

97
00:07:16,703 --> 00:07:20,299
It's what they need,
even if it is a lie.

98
00:07:24,210 --> 00:07:26,622
MALE OFFICER 1: Hey, Cap.
FEMALE OFFICER: Good to see you, sir.

99
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:29,138
- Welcome back, Captain.
- Hey, back at it.

100
00:07:29,249 --> 00:07:31,127
MALE OFFICER 2: Hey, Cap. MALE
OFFICER 3: Good to see you, boss.

101
00:07:31,151 --> 00:07:32,414
All right, listen up.

102
00:07:35,155 --> 00:07:37,266
If I'd have known I'd be
seeing your ugly mugs tonight,

103
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:38,588
I'd have stayed in the hospital.

104
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:39,785
(ALL CHUCKLING)

105
00:07:39,859 --> 00:07:43,421
Jervis Tetch, Jonathan
Crane, Jerome Valeska.

106
00:07:43,863 --> 00:07:45,195
Each of these madmen

107
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,243
has wreaked a different
kind of havoc on our city.

108
00:07:47,267 --> 00:07:50,101
Now they're on the loose, and
presumably working together,

109
00:07:50,503 --> 00:07:53,268
along with several dozen other
garden-variety psychopaths.

110
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,139
Know their MOs, their
associates, their home turf.

111
00:07:56,609 --> 00:07:57,907
Gotham needs you tonight.

112
00:07:59,179 --> 00:08:02,115
Have each other's backs, and
we'll get through this. Let's go.

113
00:08:02,182 --> 00:08:03,445
ALL: Yes, sir.

114
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:05,384
(PHONE RINGING)

115
00:08:06,886 --> 00:08:10,721
- Captain Gordon.
- Jim, Jim, Jim.

116
00:08:11,358 --> 00:08:12,519
Why so grim, Jim?

117
00:08:12,826 --> 00:08:15,295
Tetch. What do you want?

118
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:17,006
<i>I'm not playing
any of your games.</i>

119
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:19,192
No games this time.
Just some maims,

120
00:08:19,299 --> 00:08:21,699
and your own share of blames
if you don't do what I tell you.

121
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:23,167
<i>To wit, James.</i>

122
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,134
<i>Find your way to Wood
Street and James Way.</i>

123
00:08:25,305 --> 00:08:28,605
Do it, or I'm gonna
kill someone!

124
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:30,143
In case you had any doubts.

125
00:08:32,012 --> 00:08:34,052
- It's a setup.
- It's also our chance to catch him.

126
00:08:34,481 --> 00:08:36,125
If we can get Tetch, he
can lead us to Valeska.

127
00:08:36,149 --> 00:08:38,050
- I'll put a squad together...
- No.

128
00:08:38,151 --> 00:08:40,271
The force is spread too
thin looking for the escapees.

129
00:08:42,589 --> 00:08:45,081
- Let's go.
- Sure?

130
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:48,327
You said we had to have
each other's backs tonight, right?

131
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:49,761
I'm following orders, Captain.

132
00:09:03,343 --> 00:09:05,835
- I had a thought.
- I'll alert the press.

133
00:09:05,912 --> 00:09:08,677
- What if we're hypnotized?
- What?

134
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:10,342
Stick with me here.

135
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:12,343
We both listened to
Tetch on the phone.

136
00:09:12,419 --> 00:09:14,820
What if he hypno-ed us
into coming down here alone?

137
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:16,488
That would be pretty
stupid, wouldn't it?

138
00:09:16,856 --> 00:09:20,725
So, what, we're either idiots, or
we're hypnotized? Good choices.

139
00:09:22,028 --> 00:09:24,020
You did a good job with
the troops back there.

140
00:09:25,532 --> 00:09:28,525
Thanks. This is Whit
Street. Lights out.

141
00:09:32,505 --> 00:09:33,564
What the hell?

142
00:09:45,385 --> 00:09:46,648
We gotta get them out of there.

143
00:09:52,826 --> 00:09:54,203
No, don't shoot,
they're hypnotized!

144
00:09:54,227 --> 00:09:56,027
- They're hypnotized! Don't shoot!
- Back off!

145
00:09:56,796 --> 00:09:58,822
All right, buddy. Come on, hey!

146
00:09:59,299 --> 00:10:00,892
TETCH: Lo and behold,

147
00:10:01,568 --> 00:10:05,562
the bold Captain Jim Gordon,
and his rusty caboose in tow.

148
00:10:06,306 --> 00:10:08,070
You have us, Tetch, let them go.

149
00:10:08,141 --> 00:10:12,875
Do you recall when I first
came to this fair city, Jim?

150
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,880
A bawling mess,

151
00:10:15,315 --> 00:10:18,046
wanting nothing more
than to address the safety

152
00:10:18,151 --> 00:10:19,779
of my dear sister, Alice?

153
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:22,052
What's the choice
this time, Tetch?

154
00:10:22,255 --> 00:10:24,622
How do I save them?
Just tell me what you want.

155
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:28,660
What I want is my sister back!

156
00:10:28,995 --> 00:10:32,261
But you kept me from saving her.

157
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:36,793
You gave me no choice!

158
00:10:38,805 --> 00:10:43,209
So, no more choices for
you, either. No more saving.

159
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:46,478
(CHAIN RATTLING)

160
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:47,813
No!

161
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,316
(GRUNTING)

162
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,985
Soon, the bells will toll, Jim.

163
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,954
How many more
will grow cold, Jim?

164
00:10:58,191 --> 00:10:59,989
Like your soul, Jim!

165
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:04,155
How many would-be
flyers will be die-ers?

166
00:11:04,898 --> 00:11:08,130
Splattered like my
poor spitted Alice.

167
00:11:08,201 --> 00:11:12,195
When the Gotham
bells toll their full roll!

168
00:11:16,276 --> 00:11:19,440
(ALL CLUCKING)

169
00:11:26,953 --> 00:11:29,047
You said you needed
help, but you didn't say

170
00:11:29,856 --> 00:11:32,724
anything about walking
straight into the GCPD.

171
00:11:34,127 --> 00:11:35,561
You wanna bail out now?

172
00:11:36,329 --> 00:11:40,266
No, I just wanna make
sure there's no jewelry debt.

173
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:41,492
There's no debt.

174
00:11:41,668 --> 00:11:43,746
I helped you to get the jewelry
back because I want to help.

175
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:46,001
Nobody does
anything just to help.

176
00:11:46,072 --> 00:11:47,404
Fine. Once this is over,

177
00:11:47,507 --> 00:11:50,204
there will be nothing left to
settle between us. Can you do it?

178
00:11:51,778 --> 00:11:52,778
(SCOFFS)

179
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:55,875
(LOCK RATTLING)

180
00:11:55,949 --> 00:11:56,949
Okay.

181
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:00,552
(LOCK CLICKS)

182
00:12:01,087 --> 00:12:02,521
Okay, got it. Which file?

183
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:05,222
Jerome Valeska. There'll
be a red Arkham stamp on it.

184
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:06,769
Valeska? What do
you want with that nut?

185
00:12:06,793 --> 00:12:08,056
He broke out of Arkham tonight.

186
00:12:08,127 --> 00:12:09,687
Yeah. What does it
have to do with you?

187
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,649
Can you just get the file
before someone sees us?

188
00:12:18,037 --> 00:12:20,015
MAN ON RADIO: <i>The
largest single breach of security</i>

189
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:22,508
<i>in the troubled history
of Arkham Asylum</i>

190
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:26,410
<i>has led to a citywide curfew
as many of the worst criminals</i>

191
00:12:26,512 --> 00:12:29,539
<i>who have ever plagued
Gotham flood the streets.</i>

192
00:12:29,616 --> 00:12:32,347
<i>Twenty-seven deaths have
been attributed to the escapees...</i>

193
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,353
The city is going crazy pants.

194
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:37,019
Can we turn that thing off?

195
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:39,949
We could be out
there making a killing

196
00:12:40,059 --> 00:12:42,028
while the cops are
rounding up all these nutjobs.

197
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:45,623
I am gonna go nuts if we
don't turn that damn thing off!

198
00:12:46,733 --> 00:12:48,577
MAN ON RADIO: <i>Please
be aware that these escapees</i>

199
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:49,967
<i>are extremely dangerous...</i>

200
00:12:50,069 --> 00:12:51,069
(RADIO SWITCHES OFF)

201
00:12:52,272 --> 00:12:53,501
Another migraine?

202
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,471
Nothing a little
self-medication won't fix.

203
00:12:56,743 --> 00:13:00,180
And your hand?
Got a pill for that?

204
00:13:03,816 --> 00:13:04,816
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

205
00:13:07,186 --> 00:13:08,279
I'll fix it.

206
00:13:08,354 --> 00:13:11,984
I've been reading ancient
history, mysticism, philosophy,

207
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:14,287
anything that might
reference Ra's al Ghul.

208
00:13:14,394 --> 00:13:16,056
I'm sick of hearing
that charlatan's name.

209
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:18,124
He brought me back to life.

210
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:21,161
We've never even
met. Why choose me...

211
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,627
- (HIGH-PITCHED RINGING)
- (GROANS)

212
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:26,599
For all you know,
he lied to you.

213
00:13:27,407 --> 00:13:28,927
Maybe he just told
you, you were dead.

214
00:13:28,975 --> 00:13:30,775
I mean, you can't even
remember what happened.

215
00:13:32,011 --> 00:13:33,445
It hurts to remember.

216
00:13:35,748 --> 00:13:36,807
What?

217
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:40,981
The attacks I'm having,

218
00:13:42,622 --> 00:13:45,524
it's like memories are trying
to push their way into my brain,

219
00:13:45,625 --> 00:13:49,892
but when I go to touch
them, it's just this searing pain.

220
00:13:53,199 --> 00:13:56,226
- You have to let them in.
- It hurts too much.

221
00:13:57,403 --> 00:13:59,565
Listen to you, whining
like a little baby.

222
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:00,672
What?

223
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:03,005
You have been hiding here
for weeks, reading these books.

224
00:14:03,076 --> 00:14:04,653
And now, you're telling
me you might have

225
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:05,838
all the answers in your head,

226
00:14:05,912 --> 00:14:07,956
but don't want to get them
because it hurts too much?

227
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:10,540
You have no idea what
you're talking about.

228
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:12,879
No, I have no idea
who I'm talking to.

229
00:14:13,086 --> 00:14:15,817
The Barbara I know wouldn't
let anything that she's afraid of

230
00:14:15,888 --> 00:14:17,199
stand in the way
of what she wants.

231
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:21,126
Not cops, not criminals,
not blood, and not pain.

232
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:31,997
(BARBARA SIGHS)

233
00:14:37,143 --> 00:14:39,305
I remember when
it all went dark.

234
00:14:42,749 --> 00:14:47,244
It was this blinding
electric light,

235
00:14:47,353 --> 00:14:48,353
and then,

236
00:14:50,289 --> 00:14:51,289
nothing.

237
00:14:53,926 --> 00:14:55,224
And then I remember...

238
00:14:57,196 --> 00:14:58,391
(EXHALES)

239
00:14:58,931 --> 00:14:59,931
I remember...

240
00:15:02,201 --> 00:15:03,201
(SCREAMS)

241
00:15:03,703 --> 00:15:05,399
- (ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)
- (GROANS)

242
00:15:07,273 --> 00:15:09,640
RA'S: I know. I hear you.

243
00:15:11,277 --> 00:15:15,715
The world and its cruelties,
how unfair it's been to you.

244
00:15:15,882 --> 00:15:17,817
I can hear you cursing it.

245
00:15:31,531 --> 00:15:32,897
(SIZZLING)

246
00:15:39,305 --> 00:15:40,568
(GASPS)

247
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:41,938
(EXHALES HEAVILY)

248
00:15:43,242 --> 00:15:47,373
What a vital, poisonous
little mind you have.

249
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:51,577
And yet, everybody
hates you for it, don't they?

250
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,780
Yes.

251
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,591
Everybody hates me.

252
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:02,455
I don't know why.

253
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:06,761
I understand that
feeling very well, Barbara.

254
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:12,769
You are just the one
I've been looking for.

255
00:16:13,506 --> 00:16:16,999
And I have a present
for you. But it's a secret.

256
00:16:19,378 --> 00:16:22,075
You shall become
The Demon's Head.

257
00:16:23,616 --> 00:16:27,451
The League of Shadows
will be yours to command.

258
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:31,181
An army of assassins.

259
00:16:33,626 --> 00:16:36,095
The world is weak, Barbara.

260
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:39,965
And you are strong.

261
00:16:40,466 --> 00:16:44,096
Use the League to make the world

262
00:16:44,437 --> 00:16:48,033
more like you.

263
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:50,935
Barbara?

264
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:52,501
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

265
00:16:56,215 --> 00:16:59,982
I'm okay. Ra's just really...

266
00:17:02,655 --> 00:17:03,884
Understood me.

267
00:17:04,090 --> 00:17:05,649
So, you remember something?

268
00:17:06,225 --> 00:17:10,560
Yeah. It's a beacon
calling them here,

269
00:17:11,397 --> 00:17:13,832
- and they're coming.
- Who?

270
00:17:16,335 --> 00:17:18,065
The League of Shadows.

271
00:17:18,337 --> 00:17:19,430
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

272
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:22,566
All right. Hey! Same
story all around.

273
00:17:22,675 --> 00:17:24,701
Last thing they remember
is, they were driving,

274
00:17:24,810 --> 00:17:26,522
and then they were here,
and then it was cluck cluck,

275
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:29,038
here a chick, there
a chick. Any luck?

276
00:17:29,315 --> 00:17:32,080
Something bad's gonna
happen. And there's a time limit.

277
00:17:32,184 --> 00:17:33,743
That's the Gotham
bells' full roll.

278
00:17:33,853 --> 00:17:35,754
Midnight, right? That's
less than an hour.

279
00:17:35,922 --> 00:17:37,522
What's the bad thing
that's gonna happen?

280
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:39,397
I don't know. He's gonna
hypnotize more people?

281
00:17:39,492 --> 00:17:42,360
- To do what?
- "Splatted like my spitted Alice."

282
00:17:42,428 --> 00:17:45,159
His sister Alice
jumped, was impaled.

283
00:17:46,232 --> 00:17:50,033
"Flyers will become
die-ers." They'll be splatted.

284
00:17:52,505 --> 00:17:54,974
- Oh, no.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Come on.

285
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,087
(MOUTHING)

286
00:18:19,165 --> 00:18:21,634
Bruce Wayne? What
are you doing here?

287
00:18:22,168 --> 00:18:23,500
Detective Harper.

288
00:18:23,803 --> 00:18:26,796
Where is Captain
Gordon? I need to see him.

289
00:18:26,906 --> 00:18:29,808
He's out on the Arkham
break. What do you need?

290
00:18:30,042 --> 00:18:31,203
(CLATTERING)

291
00:18:32,044 --> 00:18:35,879
I need protection. Last year,
I captured Jerome Valeska.

292
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:38,474
He's clearly escaped so that
he can get his revenge on me.

293
00:18:39,285 --> 00:18:41,481
Okay, I think it's a
little bit more than that.

294
00:18:41,587 --> 00:18:43,579
I am very close friends
with Captain Gordon.

295
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:45,954
I'm sure he wants me
to be well-protected,

296
00:18:46,058 --> 00:18:48,220
but if this is a
matter of payment...

297
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,126
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Put that away.

298
00:18:50,663 --> 00:18:52,495
What do you want,
a bribery charge?

299
00:18:53,099 --> 00:18:54,795
I... I just...

300
00:18:56,435 --> 00:19:00,497
I'm sorry, I just... I'm
just really scared. (SOBS)

301
00:19:02,108 --> 00:19:03,508
I know Valeska wants me dead.

302
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,202
- I just know it.
- Take it easy, Wayne.

303
00:19:05,945 --> 00:19:09,109
All right, you can stay
here. You'll be perfectly safe.

304
00:19:09,882 --> 00:19:10,975
Okay.

305
00:19:15,354 --> 00:19:18,483
All right, Wayne.
Let's find you a seat.

306
00:19:21,861 --> 00:19:23,955
Hold on, we're
gonna get you down.

307
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,054
GORDON: Whoa, whoa, whoa.

308
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:28,518
Tetch has them booby-trapped.
If we get too close, they'll jump.

309
00:19:29,301 --> 00:19:31,099
But if we do nothing,
they jump at midnight.

310
00:19:32,872 --> 00:19:34,431
How did he get to all of them?

311
00:19:34,774 --> 00:19:36,734
And the drivers, how did
he hypnotize all of them?

312
00:19:36,809 --> 00:19:38,487
What's that matter? We
gotta help these people.

313
00:19:38,511 --> 00:19:40,071
We gotta put a net
around the building.

314
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,706
A net won't work, Harvey.

315
00:19:56,796 --> 00:20:00,233
- Do you know this diner? Zach's?
- No, why?

316
00:20:00,399 --> 00:20:01,924
Look, Valeska's uncle owns it.

317
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,201
He might know where Jerome
would go after escaping.

318
00:20:04,437 --> 00:20:06,565
Still sounds like
a cop's job to me.

319
00:20:09,608 --> 00:20:12,442
I could've killed Jerome after
he kidnapped me, and I didn't.

320
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:16,174
Any harm he does
now, I share a part of it.

321
00:20:17,116 --> 00:20:19,585
In a way, I'm responsible
for his life now.

322
00:20:21,187 --> 00:20:23,179
I can't just wait to see
what the cops will do.

323
00:20:23,456 --> 00:20:24,788
I have to get him
back to Arkham.

324
00:20:28,627 --> 00:20:29,651
What?

325
00:20:31,097 --> 00:20:34,829
Your ego, Bruce. It's huge.

326
00:20:35,434 --> 00:20:36,434
What?

327
00:20:36,769 --> 00:20:41,332
Not everything is your
fault, or your responsibility.

328
00:20:42,208 --> 00:20:43,608
Get over yourself.

329
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:46,202
It'll make you a little
easier to be around.

330
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:01,057
(CAR DOOR OPENS)

331
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:05,295
Thanks for the advice.

332
00:21:07,666 --> 00:21:08,666
(SELINA CHUCKLES)

333
00:21:13,906 --> 00:21:15,506
You sure you don't
need my help anymore?

334
00:21:16,242 --> 00:21:19,110
- We're even?
- You don't owe me anything, Selina.

335
00:21:20,346 --> 00:21:21,473
You never did.

336
00:21:34,093 --> 00:21:36,271
Are you sure you haven't heard
from your nephew, Mr. Trumble?

337
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,764
That monster killed my
sister. If I ever see him,

338
00:21:38,831 --> 00:21:40,925
his screams are
what you'll be hearing.

339
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:44,430
Just maybe give us a call
before things go that far.

340
00:21:47,573 --> 00:21:48,939
(DOOR BELL TINKLING)

341
00:21:50,276 --> 00:21:52,336
JEROME: Jeez, there's
a lot of gum under here!

342
00:21:53,579 --> 00:21:54,774
Ah.

343
00:21:57,116 --> 00:22:00,109
You're lucky those flat-foots didn't
check under the table, Uncle Zach.

344
00:22:00,186 --> 00:22:01,245
(GRUNTS)

345
00:22:02,621 --> 00:22:06,353
I mean, it's gotta be some kind of
health code violation or something.

346
00:22:10,563 --> 00:22:12,395
HARVEY: Jim, it's
happening all over the city.

347
00:22:12,498 --> 00:22:14,865
Thousands are climbing up
on roofs, more every minute.

348
00:22:15,034 --> 00:22:17,629
Drivers, people at work,
on the streets, at home.

349
00:22:18,304 --> 00:22:19,304
How's he getting to them?

350
00:22:22,875 --> 00:22:25,003
Radio. He's
broadcasting on radio.

351
00:22:25,077 --> 00:22:26,555
He must have taken
over a radio station.

352
00:22:26,579 --> 00:22:28,639
Which one? We don't
have time to hit them all.

353
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,094
The drivers who grabbed us.

354
00:22:30,382 --> 00:22:32,146
They were listening
to the same station.

355
00:22:32,218 --> 00:22:33,516
(RADIO PLAYING INDISTINCTLY)

356
00:22:33,652 --> 00:22:35,052
GORDON: XTJN here.

357
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:36,815
HARVEY: WYED.

358
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:44,963
- WEPV.
- They were all on different stations.

359
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:47,990
He must have commanded them to change
the station, so we couldn't find him.

360
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:52,996
There's only one way to
know which one he's using.

361
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:56,039
What are you doing?
No, no, no, no, Harvey.

362
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:58,040
Harvey, hey! Harvey.

363
00:22:58,677 --> 00:23:01,340
- Hey!
- WYED. Clear.

364
00:23:01,714 --> 00:23:03,649
- Harvey, no, let me go...
- KPIL.

365
00:23:03,749 --> 00:23:05,843
That toilet-paper
jingle I love so much.

366
00:23:05,951 --> 00:23:07,562
I kept Tetch out of my head
once before. I can do it again.

367
00:23:07,586 --> 00:23:09,214
XDNJ!

368
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:11,550
- (GROANS) It's that song I hate.
- Come on!

369
00:23:12,424 --> 00:23:13,551
(MUSIC PLAYING)

370
00:23:13,626 --> 00:23:14,626
JEROME: Mmm.

371
00:23:16,528 --> 00:23:17,528
Too cold.

372
00:23:18,364 --> 00:23:20,595
Ah! Too hot. Ah!

373
00:23:22,434 --> 00:23:24,869
Oh. Just right.

374
00:23:27,106 --> 00:23:28,106
Mmm.

375
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,568
You always could
cook up a storm, Unc.

376
00:23:30,876 --> 00:23:33,277
I remember back in the circus,
we used to dare each other

377
00:23:33,379 --> 00:23:36,907
to sneak into the chuck wagon
to steal one of your cookies or two.

378
00:23:37,683 --> 00:23:40,175
That reminds me of my
favorite meal you ever cooked.

379
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:41,920
(TAPS ON TABLE)

380
00:23:42,521 --> 00:23:43,750
You remember that time

381
00:23:43,856 --> 00:23:46,052
you caught me trying
to snag a snickerdoodle?

382
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:47,425
Oh.

383
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:51,294
That soup you made that
day. Mmm, <i>mamma mia.</i>

384
00:23:53,465 --> 00:23:55,127
What was the special
ingredient again?

385
00:23:56,268 --> 00:24:00,205
Ah, right. It was my hand.

386
00:24:02,041 --> 00:24:05,603
The one you dipped in a
boiling pot of chicken stock!

387
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:09,415
That smell, it was...

388
00:24:12,318 --> 00:24:16,187
Mouth-watering.
(LAUGHS MANIACALLY)

389
00:24:16,855 --> 00:24:21,190
- Almost as good as this. Mmm.
- That's a good story, nephew.

390
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:23,091
But aren't you curious
about the soup?

391
00:24:24,496 --> 00:24:27,432
- Don't tell me it's poisoned.
- (LAUGHS) Not at all.

392
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:29,667
Mmm.

393
00:24:30,002 --> 00:24:32,335
You had me worried there for
a second, Unc. (CHUCKLES)

394
00:24:32,838 --> 00:24:34,932
I set out three bowls
of soup, nephew,

395
00:24:35,174 --> 00:24:37,109
so I'd have enough
for all my guests.

396
00:24:40,779 --> 00:24:43,647
- (GROANS)
- (LAUGHS)

397
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:48,617
You remember Lunkhead from
his strongman days at the circus?

398
00:24:49,188 --> 00:24:52,022
The minute I heard you broke
out, I knew you'd be headed here.

399
00:24:52,124 --> 00:24:54,491
So, I invited good old
Lunk for some supper.

400
00:24:54,693 --> 00:24:58,186
The "just right" soup is
for him, the "cold" is for me.

401
00:24:58,697 --> 00:25:01,861
I always loved
gazpacho! (LAUGHING)

402
00:25:02,134 --> 00:25:04,603
The "too hot," that's
for you, nephew.

403
00:25:05,137 --> 00:25:06,537
(GRUNTING)

404
00:25:10,242 --> 00:25:11,835
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

405
00:25:12,544 --> 00:25:13,637
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

406
00:25:15,214 --> 00:25:17,525
I'm just saying, how could there
be a global army of assassins

407
00:25:17,549 --> 00:25:18,573
we've never heard of?

408
00:25:18,684 --> 00:25:21,347
What part of "League of
Shadows" do you not understand?

409
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:24,581
- And they're coming here?
- To me. They're coming to me.

410
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:27,569
Well, hell, Barb, shouldn't we be
getting ready for them or something?

411
00:25:27,593 --> 00:25:31,530
Oh, I'm ready. As soon as
they wanna show themselves.

412
00:25:31,830 --> 00:25:32,830
What?

413
00:25:33,565 --> 00:25:35,090
You can stop hiding.

414
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:37,526
(ELECTRICITY SURGING)

415
00:25:37,603 --> 00:25:38,935
I know you're there.

416
00:25:50,149 --> 00:25:52,243
We're here for The Demon's Head.

417
00:25:52,918 --> 00:25:54,045
Where is he?

418
00:25:57,556 --> 00:26:00,390
"She" is right here.

419
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:09,567
Harvey!

420
00:26:09,668 --> 00:26:10,761
WZPZ.

421
00:26:10,869 --> 00:26:12,547
TETCH ON RADIO: <i>Time to
climb to the tippy-top of every tower.</i>

422
00:26:12,571 --> 00:26:15,234
<i>- When the bell strikes 12:00...</i>
- Jim! WZPZ.

423
00:26:15,374 --> 00:26:17,018
<i>- Pell-mell over the edge...</i>
- Stop listening.

424
00:26:17,042 --> 00:26:18,408
That's an order, you hear me?

425
00:26:18,477 --> 00:26:19,536
Stop listening.

426
00:26:19,611 --> 00:26:21,705
- WZPZ.
- Change the station.

427
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:23,091
Come on, Harvey,
change the station.

428
00:26:23,115 --> 00:26:25,710
- (RADIO STOPS PLAYING)
- Oh, whoa.

429
00:26:27,653 --> 00:26:28,653
Wait...

430
00:26:29,988 --> 00:26:32,753
Sorry, pal, there's
something I gotta do.

431
00:26:33,892 --> 00:26:37,090
Hickory dickory dock The
cop who went up the clock

432
00:26:37,496 --> 00:26:38,623
The clock struck 12:00

433
00:26:38,730 --> 00:26:40,756
He fell pell-mell And
that was it for the cop.

434
00:26:49,808 --> 00:26:51,902
- HARPER: <i>Gotham Central.</i>
- Harper, it's Gordon.

435
00:26:52,144 --> 00:26:54,579
Cap, it is crazy here. I got
seven cops ready to jump,

436
00:26:54,646 --> 00:26:56,376
I got calls coming
in from everywhere.

437
00:26:56,548 --> 00:26:59,450
It's Tetch, he's broadcasting
from the WZPZ station.

438
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:02,247
- Okay, I'll redirect units.
<i>- No, I want all cars on the street,</i>

439
00:27:02,321 --> 00:27:05,052
ready to amplify in the
emergency G911 band.

440
00:27:05,257 --> 00:27:07,158
Radio teams on as
many roads as possible.

441
00:27:07,259 --> 00:27:08,259
And then what?

442
00:27:08,594 --> 00:27:09,721
Wait for my signal.

443
00:27:22,107 --> 00:27:23,107
(GRUNTS)

444
00:27:25,043 --> 00:27:27,444
Wait, wait, wait. No, no. No!

445
00:27:27,513 --> 00:27:28,606
(LAUGHS)

446
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:32,208
Here, nephew. Have a taste
of one of my three soups.

447
00:27:33,519 --> 00:27:35,488
JEROME: No, no, no, no. (GAGS)

448
00:27:35,554 --> 00:27:38,524
My sister had the wrong idea
with you, keeping you around.

449
00:27:38,624 --> 00:27:40,855
She should have put you
in a sack with some rocks

450
00:27:40,959 --> 00:27:42,119
and dropped you in the river!

451
00:27:42,227 --> 00:27:43,695
(COUGHS)

452
00:27:44,229 --> 00:27:45,788
Put this creep
out of our misery.

453
00:27:47,533 --> 00:27:48,762
(GROANS)

454
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,581
- What the hell are you doing?
- Get outta here, kid.

455
00:27:52,471 --> 00:27:53,471
No.

456
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:57,704
Look, kid, I appreciate a
concerned citizen and all,

457
00:27:57,809 --> 00:27:59,505
but this is Jerome Valeska,

458
00:27:59,645 --> 00:28:01,477
the psycho who broke
out of Arkham tonight.

459
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,808
And what we're doing is
giving him what he deserves.

460
00:28:04,016 --> 00:28:05,314
No one deserves that.

461
00:28:05,384 --> 00:28:07,216
- You tell him...
- Shut up.

462
00:28:07,386 --> 00:28:08,386
BRUCE: Stop.

463
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:10,781
Call the police, and
they'll come for him.

464
00:28:12,524 --> 00:28:14,686
Aw, jeez, let him go.

465
00:28:16,795 --> 00:28:17,990
And get rid of the kid.

466
00:28:25,170 --> 00:28:26,170
(LAUGHS)

467
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:30,933
Look what we left lying around.

468
00:28:31,276 --> 00:28:33,575
Enough reliving old
memories, Uncle Zach.

469
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,681
Tell me what I wanna
know. You know why I'm here.

470
00:28:35,747 --> 00:28:36,942
I don't know anything!

471
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:43,512
It's too bad we're out of soup. I
wonder what else is on the menu.

472
00:28:43,956 --> 00:28:44,956
Ah!

473
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:50,320
She's got the mark
of The Demon's Head.

474
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:54,997
- Ra's chose her.
- She doesn't even know what it is.

475
00:28:56,501 --> 00:28:58,436
I know it means I'm
your new damn leader.

476
00:28:58,537 --> 00:29:00,096
Is that all you think it is?

477
00:29:00,272 --> 00:29:02,241
Ra's didn't explain everything.

478
00:29:02,608 --> 00:29:04,167
Look at the mess
he's left us with.

479
00:29:04,610 --> 00:29:06,203
You have the mark
of The Demon's Head,

480
00:29:06,278 --> 00:29:08,907
but no woman has ever been
allowed to lead the League of Shadows.

481
00:29:09,014 --> 00:29:10,214
I'm sorry, you just said what?

482
00:29:10,249 --> 00:29:14,209
Women serve in the
League, but they do not lead.

483
00:29:14,853 --> 00:29:19,257
That's not a law, just a
stupid tradition. Ra's chose her.

484
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:22,660
We need to honor his choice.

485
00:29:22,894 --> 00:29:23,987
That's true.

486
00:29:24,963 --> 00:29:28,058
As long as you have The Demon's
Head, the League must follow you.

487
00:29:28,133 --> 00:29:29,328
Now, we're back on track.

488
00:29:29,901 --> 00:29:33,338
So, I guess I'll have to cut
The Demon's Head from you.

489
00:29:34,906 --> 00:29:36,135
(GROANS)

490
00:29:40,846 --> 00:29:42,508
Anyone else want
a shot at the title?

491
00:29:49,121 --> 00:29:52,717
- JEROME: Here comes the airplane.
- No, no, no.

492
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:55,090
No, no, I'll tell
you! I'll tell you.

493
00:29:55,294 --> 00:29:58,230
She picked St. Ignatius!
The school is St. Ignatius!

494
00:29:58,730 --> 00:30:01,757
Got it. Lost it. Write it down.

495
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,767
(BRUCE GRUNTS)

496
00:30:11,777 --> 00:30:14,576
Thanks. It's been great
catching up, Uncle Zach.

497
00:30:14,980 --> 00:30:17,415
You really brought back the
utter helplessness of childhood.

498
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:22,220
Well, see you around. I
mean, except the opposite.

499
00:30:27,459 --> 00:30:30,452
Boy billionaire Bruce
Wayne, my savior.

500
00:30:30,662 --> 00:30:33,325
Wow, I did not see
that one coming.

501
00:30:34,066 --> 00:30:35,625
(CHUCKLES)

502
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:40,670
Uh, you know, with Uncle Zach,
the beatings just never stopped.

503
00:30:40,906 --> 00:30:45,742
They went on and on.
And nobody ever helped me.

504
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:49,139
Ever.

505
00:30:50,215 --> 00:30:51,683
And that makes a man wonder,

506
00:30:52,984 --> 00:30:55,044
what the hell is wrong with you?

507
00:30:55,153 --> 00:30:57,349
(LAUGHING MANICALLY)

508
00:30:58,623 --> 00:31:01,559
The only thing funnier
than you saving my life,

509
00:31:02,194 --> 00:31:03,457
would be if I saved yours.

510
00:31:03,829 --> 00:31:04,829
No!

511
00:31:05,364 --> 00:31:06,627
No. Wait.

512
00:31:08,333 --> 00:31:09,699
What would be funnier

513
00:31:10,068 --> 00:31:13,630
is if you were choked to death
by the guy that you saved me from.

514
00:31:14,573 --> 00:31:18,169
Yeah, yeah, we'll do that
instead. Yeah, yeah, do your thing.

515
00:31:20,912 --> 00:31:22,813
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

516
00:31:27,586 --> 00:31:29,612
Almost magic hour, Gothamites.

517
00:31:29,755 --> 00:31:32,452
Time to climb to the
tippy-top of every tower.

518
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:35,356
When the bell strikes
12:00, throw yourselves,

519
00:31:35,527 --> 00:31:38,964
pell-mell over the
edge, onto your heads!

520
00:31:39,064 --> 00:31:40,396
- (GUN COCKS)
- (GASPS)

521
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:42,863
Shut up, Tetch.

522
00:31:46,972 --> 00:31:48,531
(RADIO STATIC)

523
00:31:51,209 --> 00:31:53,235
This is Captain
Gordon of the GCPD.

524
00:31:53,311 --> 00:31:55,712
<i>- Am I coming through?</i>
- You're coming through.

525
00:31:56,114 --> 00:31:57,554
<i>They can hear
you all over the city.</i>

526
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:00,779
All right, Tetch, you're
gonna tell those people

527
00:32:00,886 --> 00:32:03,378
to step back from
the ledge. No tricks.

528
00:32:03,955 --> 00:32:07,221
You go off-script, and
I'll shoot pieces off you

529
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:09,092
till you do what I say.

530
00:32:09,461 --> 00:32:13,557
I would love to do as
you command, Jim.

531
00:32:14,566 --> 00:32:17,263
But sadly, I've tied my
own hands. (CHUCKLES)

532
00:32:17,369 --> 00:32:18,428
Your hands?

533
00:32:18,537 --> 00:32:20,904
(LAUGHS)

534
00:32:22,441 --> 00:32:23,875
(SCREAMING)

535
00:32:25,977 --> 00:32:26,977
(GRUNTS)

536
00:32:27,078 --> 00:32:28,569
(PANTING)

537
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:30,742
I can't stop them.

538
00:32:30,816 --> 00:32:35,516
If anyone tells them to
save themselves, they'll jump.

539
00:32:36,988 --> 00:32:38,786
You're more than
welcome to try, Jim.

540
00:32:39,858 --> 00:32:42,020
Obey the next voice you hear!

541
00:32:42,761 --> 00:32:44,457
Tell them anything,

542
00:32:44,830 --> 00:32:47,026
it will not matter when
the bells start to ring.

543
00:32:47,132 --> 00:32:50,830
Your oh-so-callous caused the
death of my darling Alice, Jim.

544
00:32:51,870 --> 00:32:57,207
Try, and they die. Stand
by, and they all try to fly.

545
00:32:57,309 --> 00:32:58,309
(LAUGHS)

546
00:32:59,845 --> 00:33:00,845
Cap?

547
00:33:03,315 --> 00:33:06,012
<i>Cap, what do we do?
How do we save them?</i>

548
00:33:09,120 --> 00:33:10,850
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

549
00:33:10,956 --> 00:33:13,016
I could watch this
all night, Bruce!

550
00:33:14,259 --> 00:33:16,285
(LAUGHING)

551
00:33:26,872 --> 00:33:28,306
Hands off, big boy.

552
00:33:30,542 --> 00:33:32,010
(GRUNTS)

553
00:33:32,844 --> 00:33:34,335
Still don't need my help, Bruce?

554
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:36,480
Selina.

555
00:33:37,883 --> 00:33:42,014
"Selina," huh? Well,
isn't that a nice name.

556
00:33:43,154 --> 00:33:44,315
(GUN CLICKS)

557
00:33:45,657 --> 00:33:46,989
- Selina.
- No, no, no.

558
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:49,756
She's not that kind of girl.

559
00:33:51,663 --> 00:33:54,497
- Wrong answer, freak.
- Oh. That's funny, 'cause...

560
00:33:56,101 --> 00:33:57,399
(LAUGHS MANIACALLY)

561
00:34:00,639 --> 00:34:01,971
(PANTING)

562
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:06,401
Oh, all right, see
you crazy kids later!

563
00:34:06,678 --> 00:34:07,678
Ciao!

564
00:34:11,416 --> 00:34:12,975
You should've let me shoot him.

565
00:34:17,155 --> 00:34:18,646
Would've been over by now.

566
00:34:20,358 --> 00:34:22,088
Selina, I told you I'm
responsible for him.

567
00:34:23,328 --> 00:34:25,422
I can't just let him be
shot, Selina, I can't.

568
00:34:26,398 --> 00:34:28,697
I'm not taking
responsibility for this mess.

569
00:34:29,367 --> 00:34:32,303
So, let's get out of here
before the cops show up. Yeah?

570
00:34:34,806 --> 00:34:35,806
Come on.

571
00:34:39,377 --> 00:34:40,572
It's not over yet.

572
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:42,880
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

573
00:34:45,884 --> 00:34:47,147
Hey, suit yourself.

574
00:34:49,788 --> 00:34:51,222
Just don't take

575
00:34:52,824 --> 00:34:56,283
so much responsibility,
that you get yourself killed.

576
00:35:17,983 --> 00:35:19,281
(SWORDS CLANKING)

577
00:35:19,484 --> 00:35:21,612
Some legacy your
dead boyfriend left you.

578
00:35:22,420 --> 00:35:26,289
No. Ra's chose me
for a reason. I know it.

579
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,129
(BARBARA GASPS)

580
00:35:35,533 --> 00:35:40,130
You're weak. You're
all so damn weak.

581
00:35:41,606 --> 00:35:42,767
That's it.

582
00:35:44,109 --> 00:35:46,635
That is why Ra's chose me.

583
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:51,143
Because he knew I would
see how pitiful you all are.

584
00:35:52,517 --> 00:35:58,320
Afraid of change, afraid to
take orders from a woman.

585
00:35:59,557 --> 00:36:03,153
Well, listen up! I am
The Demon's Head!

586
00:36:03,728 --> 00:36:07,824
So, you sons of bitches better
start bowing down right now,

587
00:36:08,333 --> 00:36:10,529
or it's gonna get
ugly up in here.

588
00:36:23,615 --> 00:36:25,811
(RAPID GUN FIRING)

589
00:36:37,262 --> 00:36:39,925
You're right. They were weak.

590
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:42,929
And the mission of the League
of Shadows is to cull weakness.

591
00:36:43,435 --> 00:36:45,267
They were unfit
and needed to die.

592
00:36:46,071 --> 00:36:49,599
But the sisters of the
League are yours to command.

593
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:52,840
Well, it's not much
of a league now, is it?

594
00:36:54,746 --> 00:36:56,510
We're the point of
the spear, Barbara.

595
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:58,448
Hundreds will follow you.

596
00:37:00,952 --> 00:37:02,113
What the hell?

597
00:37:02,353 --> 00:37:04,254
You have no idea what
they expect from you.

598
00:37:04,856 --> 00:37:07,985
This is mine, Tabitha.
And I'm taking it.

599
00:37:13,598 --> 00:37:14,930
Tell me what I need to know.

600
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:18,164
(WIND WHOOSHING)

601
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:20,364
(BELL TOLLING)

602
00:37:24,709 --> 00:37:25,836
(SIREN WAILS)

603
00:37:26,544 --> 00:37:28,513
HARPER: <i>Cap, what do we do?</i>

604
00:37:30,181 --> 00:37:31,581
(BELL CONTINUES TOLLING)

605
00:37:35,687 --> 00:37:36,848
I can't save you.

606
00:37:43,461 --> 00:37:44,656
Save each other.

607
00:37:45,563 --> 00:37:49,432
<i>Save each other.
Save each other.</i>

608
00:38:02,247 --> 00:38:03,340
HARPER: <i>It worked.</i>

609
00:38:03,748 --> 00:38:06,240
It worked. They're
stepping away.

610
00:38:06,851 --> 00:38:09,616
- (GASPS)
- What?

611
00:38:09,721 --> 00:38:11,053
I got you. I got you.

612
00:38:19,330 --> 00:38:20,958
(CHEERING)

613
00:38:22,901 --> 00:38:24,267
(SIGHS)

614
00:38:47,559 --> 00:38:50,529
Heard we got nothing from
Tetch about Valeska's plans.

615
00:38:51,129 --> 00:38:53,826
Not a word the whole time the
medics were patching him up.

616
00:38:54,465 --> 00:38:56,400
Still, 40 escapees
back in the can,

617
00:38:56,501 --> 00:38:59,061
and a lot of people with
their feet safely on the ground.

618
00:39:00,405 --> 00:39:03,307
- You need a drink.
- I don't keep it around.

619
00:39:03,741 --> 00:39:06,540
Squirrels hide
nuts for the winter.

620
00:39:07,145 --> 00:39:10,980
I got this for whenever.

621
00:39:33,972 --> 00:39:36,999
I don't belong here. I
don't deserve to be here.

622
00:39:37,242 --> 00:39:39,211
Not in this office,
not in this building.

623
00:39:41,145 --> 00:39:42,385
By rights, I should be in jail.

624
00:39:42,647 --> 00:39:44,081
No argument from me.

625
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:48,076
But say you were in jail,
sucking on your own misery,

626
00:39:48,620 --> 00:39:51,886
where would the thousands of
people you saved tonight be, huh?

627
00:39:52,457 --> 00:39:53,516
Where would I be?

628
00:39:55,093 --> 00:39:56,755
What you did tonight was heroic.

629
00:39:58,596 --> 00:40:01,122
You could've done what
I did. Anyone could have.

630
00:40:02,700 --> 00:40:04,612
You know what I was thinking
when I jumped in that car

631
00:40:04,636 --> 00:40:06,400
and I was flicking
through those channels?

632
00:40:07,105 --> 00:40:10,075
I was thinking, "I
can do this crazy thing

633
00:40:10,608 --> 00:40:14,602
""cause if it goes sideways,
Jim Gordon will save me."

634
00:40:16,047 --> 00:40:17,276
And here we are.

635
00:40:18,283 --> 00:40:19,410
Who I am,

636
00:40:21,452 --> 00:40:27,016
what I've always said I believe
in, it's like it's a lie now, Harvey.

637
00:40:28,526 --> 00:40:31,291
Feet of clay are
heavy to carry around.

638
00:40:31,963 --> 00:40:33,431
That's what the whiskey's for.

639
00:40:40,038 --> 00:40:43,531
I judged you. For a long time.

640
00:40:45,510 --> 00:40:46,808
I shouldn't have done that.

641
00:40:51,015 --> 00:40:55,146
What you know about me,
Jim, is just the tip of the iceberg.

642
00:40:57,088 --> 00:40:59,580
There are no heroes here.

643
00:41:04,195 --> 00:41:05,424
No heroes here.

644
00:41:09,767 --> 00:41:10,767
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

645
00:41:10,835 --> 00:41:11,835
Yeah?

646
00:41:13,204 --> 00:41:15,799
Got the Wayne kid on line
three. Something about Valeska.

647
00:41:18,009 --> 00:41:19,009
(DOOR CLOSES)

648
00:41:19,777 --> 00:41:23,305
- GORDON: <i>Bruce, are you okay?</i>
- I saw Jerome Valeska tonight.

649
00:41:23,681 --> 00:41:24,944
- He killed his uncle.
- What?

650
00:41:25,183 --> 00:41:27,345
<i>He was looking for the
name of a school, St. Ignatius.</i>

651
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:29,078
- Why?
- I'm on my way to find out.

652
00:41:29,253 --> 00:41:30,846
<i>No, wherever you are, stay put.</i>

653
00:41:30,955 --> 00:41:32,924
Valeska is my problem
as much as anyone's.

654
00:41:33,124 --> 00:41:34,684
<i>- I'm going after him.</i>
- Damn it, Bruce.

655
00:41:34,792 --> 00:41:36,488
Stay the hell away
from that madman.

656
00:41:36,661 --> 00:41:38,254
I'll see you at
St. Ignatius, Jim.

657
00:41:38,763 --> 00:41:40,527
- You can yell at me there.
<i>- Bruce...</i>

658
00:41:40,798 --> 00:41:41,798
(LINE DISCONNECTS)

659
00:41:42,266 --> 00:41:43,359
Kid in trouble again?

660
00:41:43,468 --> 00:41:46,165
More than he can
handle. Let's go.

661
00:41:56,214 --> 00:41:57,341
(TIRES SCREECHING)

662
00:41:59,684 --> 00:42:00,708
(GASPS)

663
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:08,656
(SCREAMING)

664
00:42:17,769 --> 00:42:20,329
How do you like the
new threads? Hmm?

665
00:42:20,972 --> 00:42:23,305
Oh, speechless, I know.

666
00:42:23,508 --> 00:42:24,635
(GASPS)

667
00:42:25,209 --> 00:42:27,804
CRANE: You look
a fright, Mr. Tetch.

668
00:42:27,879 --> 00:42:30,007
Somewhat lame,
my dear Mr. Crane.

669
00:42:30,081 --> 00:42:34,485
But I do confess pure joy in
besting Jimmy boy with our ploy.

670
00:42:34,585 --> 00:42:37,521
Yeah, yeah, you did a great
job keeping Gordon occupied,

671
00:42:37,588 --> 00:42:40,057
meanwhile, Crane got his
Fear gas, I got my information.

672
00:42:40,158 --> 00:42:43,026
Everything is going
according to my plan.

673
00:42:43,094 --> 00:42:45,996
But no time to
palaver, gentlemen.

674
00:42:46,064 --> 00:42:47,498
We have fish to fry.

675
00:42:48,099 --> 00:42:50,364
And by "fish," I mean faces.

676
00:42:50,601 --> 00:42:52,069
Or feet.

677
00:42:53,738 --> 00:42:56,207
Ah! Something fun to fry.

678
00:42:57,408 --> 00:42:58,408
Buckle up.

679
00:43:02,780 --> 00:43:04,715
All aboard!

680
00:43:06,050 --> 00:43:07,484
Ooh, I'm coming!

681
00:43:08,219 --> 00:43:09,653
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

682
00:43:13,458 --> 00:43:14,458
English - SDH
